{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider-64 send 0xa5 was read back as 0x01 per `TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0x01 want 0xa5`, yielding `FAIL 0xdead`. Wiring in picosoc/picosoc.v:201, picosoc/picosoc.v:202 and picosoc/simpleuart.v:20 shows divider/data path into simpleuart, so loopback should match. Root cause in excerpt line 46 is `reg [2:0] send_bitcnt` which cannot hold 10-bit UART frame count and truncates 10 to 2, cutting transmit short and corrupting loopback data to 0x01.",
"patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -45,4 +45,4 @@
 	reg [9:0] send_pattern;
-	reg [2:0] send_bitcnt;
+	reg [3:0] send_bitcnt;
 	reg [31:0] send_divcnt;
 	reg send_dummy;
",
"expected": "tohost PASS (replacing FAIL 0xdead), TRAP gone, uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

